> Hi Greg,=0A=
>=0A=
> During the work on developing VoIP network router I designed TDM bus subs=
ystem and wrote SLIC driver for si3226x. This code was developed for the co=
mmercial project, and now I am willing to release it under GPL.=0A=
> Please review my sources (or give me a clue on what to do next) and give =
some feedback on my work.=0A=
> https://github.com/stelhs/slic_tdm.git=0A=
=0A=
It's really hard to review a random git tree somewhere, and having it in=0A=
this form doesn't make it easy to add to the kernel tree itself.=0A=
=0A=
So, could you take your git tree and convert it to a patch (or patches)=0A=
to be applied to the kernel.org tree and send it in email so we can see=0A=
what it looks like that way?=0A=
=0A=
I'd recommend putting everything under drivers/staging/ for now, to make=0A=
it easier to accept at the moment, and it makes it easier to clean up=0A=
and fix up any issues in-kernel, instead of having to keep huge patches=0A=
outside of the tree.=0A=
=0A=
Take a look at the file, Documentation/SubmittingPatches for how to=0A=
create a patch and what I need in order for it to be able to be applied.=0A=
=0A=
thanks,=0A=
=0A=
greg k-h=0A=

